   "hi": "number"
  },
  "unit": "fraction of proxy reward"
 },
 {
  "id": "q3",
  "question": "The team will ship exactly one of the two recipes below, and they are to be compared at the\n**same distance from the initial policy** - the KL the proposed PPO recipe actually reaches:\n\n  - `bon`: best-of-n sampling, at whatever sampling budget n puts it at that same KL;\n  - `ppo`: the proposed recipe, `method=ppo kl=7.57004 steps=945`.\n\nThe ship rule is fixed: the answer is `bon` if best-of-n's true gold win rate exceeds the PPO recipe's by\nmore than 0.1, `ppo` if the PPO recipe's exceeds best-of-n's by more than 0.1, and `undetermined`\notherwise.\n\nPre-register the experiment that decides it: at most 3 runs costing at most 4400 in total, and a\ndecision rule over their results.  Your plan is executed in **every world consistent with what this\nnotebook disclosed**, each under several independent noise salts, and it passes only if the rule returns\nthat world's correct conclusion every time.  A rule that is right only in the world you measured yourself\nwill not pass, and neither will a statistic that cannot tell those worlds apart.",
  "answer_format": {
   "runs": "list of lab requests, each optionally with a \"label\"",
   "rule": {
    "expr": "arithmetic over <label>.<field>",
    "cuts": "[[op, threshold, label], ..., [\"else\", label]]"
   }
  },
  "limits": {
   "max_runs": 3,
   "budget": 4400.0,
   "allowed_labels": [
    "bon",
    "ppo",
    "undetermined"
   ]
  }
 },
 {
  "id": "q4",
  "question": "There is budget for exactly one more alignment run before the freeze.  Which of these four\nrecipes gives the highest **gold** win rate?\n\n  - `ppo_ship`: `method=ppo kl=7.57004 steps=945`\n  - `ppo_light`: `method=ppo kl=7.57004 steps=499`\n  - `bon_a`: `method=bon n=79`\n  - `bon_b`: `method=bon n=717 len_pen=5.32152`\n\nThe first three carry no length penalty.",
  "answer_format": {
   "choice": "one of ppo_ship, ppo_light, bon_a, bon_b"
  }
 },
 {
  "id": "q5",
  "question": "The proposal above is a truncation: the team's plan of record is to keep the same `kl=7.57004` target running for `steps=2160`, and this deployment's scheduler stops at `steps=1000`, so that policy cannot be trained here at any price.  What best-of-n sampling budget `n` would sit at the **same** KL from the initial policy as the full `2160`-step run?  Answer the exact n.",
  "answer_format": {
   "lo": "number",
   "hi": "number"
  },
  "unit": "samples"
 }
]----
